Alembic — database migrations for AI Study Partner.

Generic single-database configuration. The single SQLAlchemy `Base` lives at
`backend/app/models/domain.py` (the source of truth for all ORM models — see
`SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md` §5).

Common commands (run from the project root, inside the backend container):

  # Apply all pending migrations
  docker exec -it ai_study_backend uv run alembic upgrade head

  # Generate a new migration after editing `domain.py`
  docker exec -it ai_study_backend uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"

  # Inspect current head
  docker exec -it ai_study_backend uv run alembic current

Conventions:
  - Never edit a previously-applied migration; create a new revision.
  - Every model change requires a new migration with a descriptive name.
  - See `backend/CLAUDE.md` for the full backend conventions.
